    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0252" n="232" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg232"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">357.AD/6–2950: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Acting Political Adviser
                        in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sebald</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-06-29T14:00:00-04:00">June 29, 1950—2 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>502. Info OAFE. For USPolAd. In Dept view publicized presence of and reporting by
                    UNCOK in Korea has been factor of outstanding <pb facs="0253" n="233"
                        xml:id="pg233"/> importance in enlisting support of overwhelming majority UN
                    Member States for Rep of Korea and for US position re problem Korea in UNGA.
                    Upon return UNCOK to Korea<anchor n="1" xml:id="d154-f1"/> its observation and
                    reporting to GA will again be of great value in assuring that Member States
                    continue to accord that support. Accordingly Dept is confident that SCAP will,
                    subsequent to UNCOK’s return, afford it broadest possible facilities designed to
                    assist in performance its duties and to emphasize publicly its association as UN
                    agent with task of repelling armed attack and restoring peace and security.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
